## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to join across topics with late-arriving updates, implement a TTL-based in-memory state store, and maintain at-least-once semantics while isolating enrichment logic.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-topic enrichment and per-key state
- TTL-based eviction and stale data handling
- Out-of-order arrival tolerance and idempotent processing
- Error routing to dead_letters and offset management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: in-memory profile store with TTL
class ProfileStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) { this.ttlMs = ttlMs; this.map = new Map(); }
  update(userId, profile) { this.map.set(userId, { profile, t: Date.now() }); }
  get(userId) {
    const e = this.map.get(userId); if (!e) return null;
    if (Date.now() - e.t > this.ttlMs) { this.map.delete(userId); return null; }
    return e.profile;
  }
}
```

